#   ..._fresh_lines_on_an_unchanged_step_report_no_progress          A-025's second case
#   ..._no_ledger_at_all_is_an_empty_roster_not_an_error             CT-004's empty input
#
# FR-025's derivation is pinned by the four threshold_* names: the constant is
# above 5x the shortest measured working batch and below half the median, so
# retuning it to a "generic constant" turns them red.
#
# GRIND cycle 4 added two sections. D-022 — a finished agent stops writing, so
# without a terminal state it ages into `stalled` and silts up needs_attention
# until the list stops being read:
#   ..._a_finished_agent_reports_done_however_long_ago_it_finished  the defect
#   ..._a_finished_agent_does_not_fill_needs_attention              its real cost
#   ..._a_resumed_agent_leaves_done_behind          terminal is the LAST line,
#                                                   not a latch on the file
# D-021 — the four INSPECT stream agents are spawned from the F2 roster, not
# from either tool in this module, so a glob over progress/ had no row for
# them at all and their silence was indistinguishable from success:
#   ..._expected_stream_agents_with_no_ledger_are_reported        the defect
